[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:A Glass Envelope]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.79]How did Jane receive a letter from a stranger? | 简是怎样收到一个陌生人来信的？
[00:16.79]My daughter, Jane, never dreamed of receiving a letter from a girl of her own age in Holland. | 我的女儿简从未想过会接到荷兰一位同龄姑娘的来信。
[00:26.87]Last year, we were travelling across the Channel and Jane put a piece of paper with her name and address on it into a bottle. | 去年，当我们横渡英吉利海峡时，简把写有她姓名和住址的一张纸条装进了一只瓶子。
[00:37.71]She threw the bottle into the sea. | 她将瓶子扔进了大海。
[00:41.19]She never thought of it again, but ten months later, she received a letter from a girl in Holland. | 此后她再没想起过那只瓶子，但10个月以后，她收到了荷兰一位姑娘的来信。
[00:49.93]Both girls write to each other regularly now. | 现在这两位姑娘定期通信了。
[00:54.19]However, they have decided to use the post office. | 然而她们决定还是利用邮局。
[00:59.72]Letters will cost a little more, but they will certainly travel faster. | 不过信件的费用稍贵一些，但肯定走得快多了。
